  "services": {
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Released in 1975 by Polydor, Tommy (Original Soundtrack Recording) is a rock opera soundtrack featuring performances by various artists, most notably members of The Who alongside actors from the film adaptation of the band’s landmark concept album. The music blends hard rock, pop, and theatrical elements, showcasing Pete Townshend’s signature songwriting and synthesizer work, while elaborate choral arrangements and orchestral flourishes underscore the cinematic scope. The album includes both re-recorded versions of the original Tommy songs and new tracks such as “Champagne” and “Mother and Son,” tailored for the film’s narrative.\n\nAs a companion to Ken Russell’s 1975 film, this soundtrack occupies a unique place in The Who’s discography, bridging their rock opera legacy with the world of stage and screen. While the original 1969 Tommy album is widely regarded as a classic, the 1975 soundtrack is notable for its all-star cast—including Roger Daltrey, Ann-Margret, and Oliver Reed—and its expanded musical palette. The album received mixed critical reception upon release, praised for its ambition and production but sometimes criticized for straying from the raw energy of the original. Commercially, it reached a broad audience, benefiting from the film’s popularity and the enduring appeal of The Who’s music.",
      "generated_at": "2025-11-27T10:26:00.781960",
      "model": "sonar",
      "source": "perplexity"
    }
  },
